            "key": "SU2NCKQ8",
            "version": 55,
            "parentItem": "VPLDNP6C",
            "itemType": "note",
            "note": "<div data-schema-version=\"8\"><p>In this paper, it proposes, Local and Stitch. This method merges fine tuned models’ parameters by identifying a small set of task related parameter regions and merge them into the shared pretrained model.<span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\"> The paper shows that these localized regions are extremely small around&nbsp;</span><strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">1% of total parameters</span></strong><span style=\"color: rgb(0, 0, 0)\">. However, the merged model still recover nearly all finetuned performance, which leads to performance improvement over multiple benchmarks. It also argues that this approach helps preserve pretrained knowledge, enables strong model compression, and makes continual skill composition more efficient.&nbsp;</span></p>\n</div>",
            "tags": [],
            "relations": {},
            "dateAdded": "2026-04-02T16:32:40Z",
            "dateModified": "2026-04-02T16:35:44Z"
        }
